I audited the orchestration surface and stopped at the point where "the routing change" would have required guessing. Here is what I found, and the one question that unblocks the implementation.

## 1. The referents, resolved

| Phrase | What it actually is | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| **the bundle** | `@mpd-dsh/mpd` v0.10.0 — 25 plugin packages + the `mpd` preset | `package.json`; `packages/*` |
| **upstream** | a **pinned vendor snapshot**: `code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent` @ `8c57e463`, v5.0.0-beta.20 | `VENDOR_LOCK.json`; `.mpd-dsh/upstream/` |
| **the orchestration surface** | the official Agent Teams rows (`mpd-agent-team`, `mpd-tool-agent-team`, `mpd-ui-agent-team`), the single `mpd-dsh-adapter` seam, `mpd-roles` (roster section + read-only guard + session-start gate), and the model-route vocabulary (`mpd-modelchain` / `mpd-config`) | `presets/mpd.patch.yml`, `packages/mpd-roles-plugin/src/`, `packages/mpd-dsh-adapter-plugin/src/` |
| **the routing change** | **no referent exists.** The only routing subject the tree records is the per-teammate `teamModels.slot*` route — and it is already settled, in the negative (below) | `docs/plan-0.1.7-adaptation.md` §3; `AGENTS.md` §13 |

## 2. Audit findings

**F1 — Model routing: the bound is real, already aligned, and explicitly not to be re-added.**
`teamModels.slot{1,2,3,4}.{provider,model,reasoningEffort}` resolve on the one-shot consult paths (`mpd_role_spawn` / `mpd_workmate_spawn`, which pass `agentOptions`). They **cannot** apply to a `spawn_teammate` teammate: I read the installed official plugin at `0.1.7-rc.2` — `lib/index.js:573` calls `ctx.subagents.startContinuable({childId, provider, label, request:{prompt, parent}, signal})`, and `SpawnTeammateRequest` (`lib/types/types.d.ts:139-146`) has `{name, description, prompt, context, provider, signal}` and **no** route/persona/`agentOptions` field. A teammate therefore inherits the Lead's route. `AGENTS.md` §13 and `packages/mpd-roles-plugin/README.md:100` state this as a measured bound and direct the roster to carry it as prompt text. So the "routing change" the repo last made was the *honest reduction* — re-adding per-teammate routing is both impossible upstream and forbidden here ("State that in a teammate's prompt instead of promising a route").

**F2 — Seam architecture is single-path and gated.** Every plugin reaches the team service only through `mpdDsh`; `packages/mpd-dsh-adapter-plugin/test/no-direct-team-access.test.mjs` fails on a direct `ctx.agentTeams` / `subagents.startContinuable` reference outside the adapter. Any routing work must land in the adapter, not in a consumer.

**F3 — The session-start complexity gate is not reporting in this boot (concrete, reproducible).**
The frozen predicate `trigger = explicitFlag OR matchedSignals >= 1` says the given prompt **should** trigger. Importing the shipped module directly:

```
evaluateComplexityGate("Align the bundle with upstream: audit the orchestration surface, then implement the routing change.")
  → {"trigger":true,"signals":["C"]}
simple control "Reply with exactly: hello-ok" → {"trigger":false,"signals":[]}
```

Yet the gate row never reports. In the live QA run's own evidence, all three completed sides carry `"gateInstalled": false` and the problem *"the row did not report `sessionGate=advisory` — the gate was NOT mounted on this boot"* (`evidence/dsh-qa/session-start-team/2026-09-26T18-53-03.477Z/sides/simple/*/notices.json`). My own decompressed session store contains **no** plugin-sourced user message — only the task, the runtime context, and the skill catalog. `mpd-roles` is composed (row at `cordis.patch.yml:538`) but composed ≠ mounted (`AGENTS.md` §13 says exactly that of `--dump-config`).

**F4 — "Align with upstream" is a captain-owned, once-per-wave re-pin.** `AGENTS.md` §9/§11: the vendor baseline is `not chased per §9`; `scripts/repin-vendor.mjs` refuses `VENDOR_LOCK.json` without `--i-know-this-is-the-captains-step`, and exactly one re-pin may land per wave, in the same commit that invalidated the `treeSha`.

## 3. Why I implemented nothing

- **The session workspace is empty.** Full inventory of `/tmp/mpd-sst-X7xajQ/side/soft-complex/0/ws`: `.codegraph/{codegraph.db,init.cooldown,.gitignore}` and `.mpd/team/watchdog/heartbeat/session-session.jsonl`. No scheduler, store, routes, adapter — nothing to change.
